## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a secure, scalable per-tenant ingestion path using presigned URLs, cross-account access, and KMS without exposing tenant data.

## Key Concepts
- S3 presigned URLs
- Per-tenant prefixes
- Cross-account IAM roles with least privilege
- SSE-KMS per-tenant key
- Onboarding/offboarding and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
import { S3Client, PutObjectCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-s3";
import { getSignedUrl } from "@aws-sdk/s3-request-presigner";

const s3 = new S3Client({region: "us-east-1"});
async function presign(tenantId, objectKey) {
  const cmd = new PutObjectCommand({Bucket: "central-bucket",
    Key: `tenants/${tenantId}/${objectKey}`});
  return await getSignedUrl(s3, cmd, { expiresIn: 900 });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit usage of these URLs?
- How would you revoke access if a tenant is compromised?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses design of scalable, compliant pipelines with immutability, latency, DR, and cost in AWS.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Firehose, S3, Object Lock, SSE-KMS
- Glue Streaming, Lambda, DynamoDB state
- DLQ, cross-region replication, CloudWatch

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-idempotent Lambda sketch
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();
exports.handler = async (evt) => {
  const key = { id: evt.id };
  const exists = await ddb.get({TableName:'Processed', Key:key}).promise();
  if (exists.Item) return;
  await ddb.put({TableName:'Processed', Item:{id: evt.id, t: Date.now()}}).promise();
  // enrich data
};
```

